  "summary": "A technique where diluted paint is soaked directly into unprimed canvas to create luminous color fields.",
  "description": "Characterized by thin washes of color that soak into the canvas fabric, creating luminous, stained areas without obscuring the canvas texture. Developed by Helen Frankenthaler, it allowed for subtle color transitions and a more intimate scale than other Color Field approaches.",
